1. Purpose

This file contains the twenty-two research questions governing Web4 name, image, likeness, voice, biography, persona, digital-replica, digital-twin, synthetic-media, and agentic-rights systems.

The questions define the research agenda for:

* identity-vector classification;
* human authorization;
* machine-readable consent;
* persona activation;
* modification and sublicensing;
* suspension;
* revocation;
* expiration;
* termination;
* persistent digital artifacts;
* false endorsements;
* impersonation;
* synthetic-media disclosure;
* emergency safeguards;
* responsibility for agent output;
* model updates;
* posthumous rights;
* minors;
* and vulnerable persons.

This file does not declare jurisdiction-specific legal rights.

It identifies the questions that must be investigated before the Web4 NIL framework can be treated as legally, technically, or operationally mature.

