RQ66 — Authorization Lifecycle

Research Question

How should revocation, suspension, expiration, amendment, and termination differ?

Short Title

Consent Lifecycle Events

Definitions to Develop

Suspension

Temporary disabling of permitted use while authorization remains unresolved or conditionally preserved.

Revocation

Withdrawal of previously granted authorization, subject to applicable contract and law.

Expiration

Automatic end of authorization at the defined date or condition.

Amendment

Authorized modification of one or more terms.

Termination

End of the governing agreement or relationship.

Purpose

These events may have different legal, operational, and technical effects and must not be used interchangeably.

